Statement: "After that commit the password is gone from the repository, so it does not need to be changed."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. Removing the file from the next commit leaves all 41 earlier versions in the history, on every clone and fork, and in any CI cache. Treat the value as leaked: rotate the password first, then clean the history if you must (a rewrite does not reach existing clones). Terraform state stores resource attributes in plain text, secrets included, which is why it belongs in an encrypted, access-controlled backend and why secrets are better kept out of Terraform (for RDS, `manage_master_user_password` keeps the password in Secrets Manager).', 1, 5
